        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain replace-mode filtering in model picker",
        "body": "Closes #104545\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `models.mode: \"replace\"` filters the model catalog, the Control UI showed the resulting models without explaining why other bundled or discovered models might be absent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nConfigured model-list responses now carry additive `catalogMode: \"replace\"` metadata. The chat model picker and Quick Settings use that metadata to explain that model settings are filtering the catalog, without claiming that every visible row was explicitly configured. Full-catalog (`view: \"all\"`) responses do not carry the hint metadata.\n\nThe picker action opens the Models section directly at `/settings/ai-agents?section=models#config-section-models`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can tell that local model settings are filtering the catalog and can navigate directly to the relevant settings instead of treating an absent model as an upstream support problem.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto current `main` at `8ff4f0161fc`; exact pushed head: `89550ae8780`.\n- The rebase conflicts were limited to `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-pane.ts` and `ui/src/i18n/.i18n/catalog-fallbacks.json`. The chat-pane resolution preserves current main's session-projection import plus this PR's model-settings link. The fallback catalog was regenerated with the documented keyless `pnpm ui:i18n:baseline` flow; no non-English locale bundle changed.\n- `git range-diff` confirms the reviewed implementation remains equivalent apart from current-main context, the preserved session-projection import, and the regenerated fallback source hash.\n- Focused Gateway regressions: 2 files, 48 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/models.test.ts`\n- Focused Control UI regressions: 5 files, 263 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm --dir ui exec vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts src/pages/chat/models.test.ts src/pages/config/quick.test.ts src/pages/model-providers/data.test.ts`\n- Targeted Chromium replace-mode regression: 1 passed, 6 skipped.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts -t 'explains model filtering in replace mode'`\n- `pnpm protocol:check` passed with generated TypeScript, Swift, and Kotlin outputs stable.\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:verify` passed with the keyless fallback baseline valid.\n- Full `pnpm lint --threads=8` passed.\n- `oxfmt --check` passed on every changed supported file. The repository-wide `pnpm format:check` currently reports only unchanged current-main `extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts`, outside this PR.\n- `pnpm check:max-lines-ratchet`, `pnpm deadcode:unused-files`, and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Desktop 1280x900 and mobile 393x852 proof remains in the earlier immutable proof comment. The rebased implementation preserves the same visible hint and Manage models navigation behavior.\n\nBefore: the UI silently presented the filtered catalog.\n\nAfter: the picker and Quick Settings state, \"Replace mode filters models according to your model settings,\" and link directly to the Models settings section.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex was used to implement, test, and review this change. No agent transcript is attached.\n",
        "branch": "agent/model-picker-replace-mode-hint",
